> 1 - Does anyone have a good spellbook management technique? My problem
> last game was all my spells timed out and I had read the books too
> many times. Unfortunately I did not know this until I attempted to
> read the books and they were 'too faded to read'.

Go faster, 60,000 turns is enough for some and 80,000 for
most. If you're playing a longer game you don't need all the
spells all the time. You may need to reserve a magic marker
and a couple of blank spellbooks for the few you consider
essential. Probably cure sickness, finger of death and magic
missile would do for the planes.

You can get lots of extra spellbooks by sacrificing until
you can pray, pray, and start over.

I picked up a tip earlier to Name (not individually) a book
with the number of turns when you read it so you could use \
to figure out if it was going to run out soon.

